[{:db/id 17592186161913 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9680f992-2dc3-5aac-87ab-7495dd858cd3" "question-29d96c1a-468a-51d2-98aa-0f7dc0a4e8a2" "question-96c0c518-549b-50cc-9848-33bcafaa76df" "question-7422bd44-ce95-5bfa-9bb0-a1ce83943ba4" "question-5b31bb9a-c9ff-580a-a94b-41f92daf9665"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161716 :question/worked-solution "We have $\\dfrac{2}{5}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{6}{20}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/f0/f087c076a86b5bab709af23db87d63ed66363d4d580c23dc453573f264fb28bc.png)\n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{5} \\times \\dfrac{3}{4} = \\dfrac{6}{20}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161914 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-632bdc32-0439-5085-9d25-08594d5e1d55" "question-077086cd-6950-5cf9-9941-247f49a033f6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161717 :question/worked-solution "We have $\\dfrac{3}{4}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{9}{20}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/31/31badccda3cc3548e2bdc40158e88d32feddcf92b8fdd4d4ae18f08396ca8cfc.png)\n\nThe shape on the right-hand side is split into $5$ equal parts by horizontal lines.\nSo, the shaded part on the right is $\\dfrac{\\color{blue}3}{5}$ of the shaded part on the left. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{4} \\times \\dfrac{\\color{blue}3}{5} = \\dfrac{9}{20}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\color{blue}3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161915 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-38177e16-9481-59a0-81e0-6e58dd2d54cc" "question-3670d807-18c1-5863-9538-ea1e1c221139" "question-57a610e6-33e6-576c-945d-3d21aceab52a" "question-788dd74c-3739-5a59-8086-0bbefef81874" "question-bb1e2438-c215-5910-b317-5383757437a3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161718 :question/worked-solution "In the model, we have $\\dfrac{2}{3}$ on the left.\n\nSince we need to multiply by $\\dfrac{\\color{red}4}{\\color{blue}5}$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}5$ equal parts horizontally and ensure that $\\color{red}4$ of the parts remain shaded.\n\n![](images/97/978789f7aed1ea0e0dc8794aaeb00a3829168101e792129e72c0585fac43ebe2.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we see that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{8}{15}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore, the missing picture is as follows:\n\n![](images/fa/faf527aba9974aa23b9a5bffd8fc8f54a2135fce10bf2d09a7133556ab4b95e3.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161916 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fafe9aa8-8740-56ea-b7ab-0d923faf8e05" "question-b46d3c89-f90b-5c6e-b0cf-a3937a245659" "question-c5028fee-c0a7-51db-9d38-ca5458f022a3" "question-74e4d9c3-fbbb-5584-a3c7-049770dc6830" "question-5cff78bb-33e7-50fb-97b0-b041b86a2216"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161719 :question/problem "![](images/60/6026c90a1101bf484ab649dcb35964ae4b136fc7784e384d1cf5d90ea47a96a2.png)\n\nUse the model above to calculate $\\dfrac{2}{6} \\times \\dfrac{3}{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we need to multiply by $\\dfrac{\\color{red}3}{\\color{blue}4}$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}4$ equal parts horizontally and ensure that $\\color{red}3$ of the parts remain shaded.\n\n![](images/0f/0f7c5ff7155c00a811c744606ee039e764c6ded16f214a163b6d5d4a481e633b.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we see that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{6}{24}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{6} \\times \\dfrac{3}{4} = \\dfrac{6}{24}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-9680f992-2dc3-5aac-87ab-7495dd858cd3" :question/id #uuid "9680f992-2dc3-5aac-87ab-7495dd858cd3" :question/math-academy-id "q-92180" :question/problem "![](images/f0/f0faa033ca75ef5ea9b931ea4158ac735405686beb2befb03042381d7a15695e.png)\n\nWhat multiplication problem is represented by the model above?" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\frac{3}{4}$ on the left and $\\frac{12}{20}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/45/45b3351533a3b0d1fb0e9249d5f33