/id "answer-50213a84-110c-5c3c-937f-6883bdbb3391" :answer/id #uuid "50213a84-110c-5c3c-937f-6883bdbb3391" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8fc7b230-66fa-55ec-99fd-8284eb428aed" :answer/id #uuid "8fc7b230-66fa-55ec-99fd-8284eb428aed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a157b2b4-84d6-5ca8-8834-309f6cc75a1b" :answer/id #uuid "a157b2b4-84d6-5ca8-8834-309f6cc75a1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f05370b1-95d4-583a-a2d3-cad205680c9e" :answer/id #uuid "f05370b1-95d4-583a-a2d3-cad205680c9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e5b711d7-fd97-588e-a52b-d5d0bf1d7892" :answer/id #uuid "e5b711d7-fd97-588e-a52b-d5d0bf1d7892" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163366 :tutorial/content "We can use fraction models to multiply any two fractions. \n\nLet's figure out how to use models to compute the following product:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{5} \\times \\dfrac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nWe start with the model of $\\dfrac{3}{5}.$\n\n![](images/06/06869533fb9eae08e88187c0965c9683c3b00e8cf269b121f416ce7f473ad508.png)\n\nSince we need to multiply by $\\dfrac{\\color{red}2}{\\color{blue}3}$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}3$ equal parts *horizontally*. But this time, we keep the shaded pieces in the bottom $\\color{red}2$ rows.\n\n![](images/0c/0c449cdff6dabfd6599925b0d450ab2d579ce49d2729b9a98fe63bb8992a850d.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we see that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{6}{15}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{5} \\times \\dfrac{2}{3} = \\dfrac{6}{15}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162206 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
